module mt-district-court-civil.civil

start complaint-filed

state complaint-filed: "Complaint filed" by applicant cite "M. R. Civ. P. 3"
{
  note "A civil action is commenced by filing a complaint with the court (M. R. Civ. P. 3). Periods in this package are stated, not counted: Rule 6(a) excludes the trigger day, counts every day, and includes the last day unless it is a Saturday, Sunday or legal holiday, Montana's legal holidays including state general election day and days the Governor declares (M. R. Civ. P. 6(a)); 3 days are added after service under Rule 5(b)(2)(C)-(F) (M. R. Civ. P. 6(d)). The filing fee is not stated in the vendored rules. The earlier outline named no leading decision for this step."
  edge-complaint-filed-served "Summons and complaint served" -> answer-due {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 4"
  }
  edge-complaint-filed-unserved "Not served within three years" -> dismissed-unserved {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 4(t)"
  }
}

terminal dismissed-unserved: "Dismissed without prejudice for want of service" outcome [loss, dismissal] cite "M. R. Civ. P. 4(t)"
{
  note "A plaintiff must accomplish service within three years after filing the complaint; absent an appearance by the defendant, the court on motion or on its own must dismiss the action without prejudice if the plaintiff fails to do so (M. R. Civ. P. 4(t)(1))."
}

decision answer-due: "Answer, motion or default" by office cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(a)"
{
  note "A defendant serves an answer within 21 days after being served with the summons and complaint; the State of Montana, a state agency, or an officer or employee sued in an official capacity within 42 days after service on the attorney general; a state officer or employee sued individually for acts on the state's behalf within 42 days after service on the officer or employee or on the attorney general, whichever is later. A Rule 12 motion alters the period: if the court denies it or postpones its disposition until trial, the responsive pleading is due within 14 days after notice of the court's action (M. R. Civ. P. 12(a))."
  edge-answer-due-default "No answer or defense" -> default-entered {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 55(a)"
  }
  edge-answer-due-motion "Rule 12(b) motion" -> pleading-motion {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
  }
  edge-answer-due-answer "Answer served" -> discovery { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(a)" }
}

decision pleading-motion: "Motion to dismiss decided" by court cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
{
  note "The defenses of Rule 12(b)(1)-(7) may be made by motion, which must be made before pleading if a responsive pleading is allowed (M. R. Civ. P. 12(b)). If the motion is denied or deferred to trial, the answer is due within 14 days after notice of the court's action (M. R. Civ. P. 12(a)(4)). The earlier outline named no Montana pleading-standard decision; none is vendored."
  edge-pleading-motion-granted "Granted" -> dismissed { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(b)" }
  edge-pleading-motion-amend "Leave to amend" -> amend { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 15(a)" }
  edge-pleading-motion-denied "Denied: answer within 14 days of notice" -> discovery {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(a)"
  }
}

state amend: "Amended pleading" by applicant cite "M. R. Civ. P. 15(a)"
{
  note "A party may amend once as a matter of course within 21 days after serving the pleading or, if a responsive pleading is required, 21 days after service of a responsive pleading or of a Rule 12(b), (e) or (f) motion, whichever is earlier; otherwise only with the opposing party's written consent or the court's leave, freely given when justice so requires. A required response is due within the time remaining on the original pleading or 14 days after service of the amendment, whichever is later (M. R. Civ. P. 15(a))."
  edge-amend-tested "Amended pleading tested again" -> pleading-motion {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
  }
}

terminal dismissed: "Dismissed on the pleadings" outcome [win, dismissal] cite "M. R. Civ. P. 12(b)"
{
  note "Outcome from the defending side. Whether the dismissal is with or without prejudice is stated in the order; the vendored rules fix no default for a Rule 12(b) dismissal."
}

decision default-entered: "Default" by court cite "M. R. Civ. P. 55(a)"
{
  note "When a party against whom affirmative relief is sought has failed to plead or otherwise defend, and that is shown by affidavit or otherwise, the clerk must enter its default (M. R. Civ. P. 55(a)). The clerk enters judgment for a sum certain against a defendant defaulted for not appearing who is neither a minor nor incompetent; in other cases the party applies to the court, and a party that has appeared is served written notice of the application at least 7 days before the hearing (M. R. Civ. P. 55(b)). A default against the State, its officers, agencies or subdivisions requires evidence satisfying the court (M. R. Civ. P. 55(d)). The court may set aside an entry of default for good cause and a default judgment under Rule 60(b) (M. R. Civ. P. 55(c))."
  edge-default-entered-judgment "Default judgment entered" -> default-judgment {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 55(b)"
  }
  edge-default-entered-set-aside "Default set aside for good cause" -> discovery {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 55(c)"
  }
}

terminal default-judgment: "Default judgment" outcome [loss] cite "M. R. Civ. P. 55(b)"
{
  note "Outcome from the defending side."
}

state discovery: "Discovery and pretrial" by applicant cite "M. R. Civ. P. 26"
{
  note "Discovery is by deposition, interrogatories, production, examination and requests for admission (M. R. Civ. P. 26(a)); the vendored rule states no initial-disclosure period. On a party's request, the judge issues a scheduling order within 90 days, limiting the time to join parties, amend the pleadings, complete discovery and file motions (M. R. Civ. P. 16(b)). A jury is demanded by serving a written demand no later than 14 days after the last pleading directed to the issue is served, and filing it (M. R. Civ. P. 38(b))."
  edge-discovery-sj "Summary judgment motion" -> summary-judgment {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 56"
  }
  edge-discovery-trial "No dispositive motion" -> trial { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 38" }
  edge-discovery-settled "Stipulated dismissal" -> settled { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 41(a)" }
}

decision summary-judgment: "Summary judgment decided" by court cite "M. R. Civ. P. 56(c)"
{
  note "Unless the court orders otherwise, a party may move at any time; the opponent files a response and opposing affidavits within 21 days after the motion is served or a responsive pleading is due, whichever is later; the movant may reply within 14 days after the response is served; and the right to a hearing is waived unless requested within 14 days after the time for a reply expires. Judgment should be rendered if there is no genuine issue as to any material fact and the movant is entitled to judgment as a matter of law (M. R. Civ. P. 56(c)). The earlier outline named no Montana summary-judgment decision; none is vendored."
  edge-summary-judgment-granted "Granted" -> judgment-entered {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 56(c)"
  }
  edge-summary-judgment-denied "Denied" -> trial { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 56(c)" }
}

state trial: "Trial by jury or by the court" by court cite "M. R. Civ. P. 38"
{
  note "A party waives a jury trial unless its demand is properly served and filed (M. R. Civ. P. 38(d)). At least two-thirds of a jury may render a verdict (M. R. Civ. P. 48). A renewed motion for judgment as a matter of law is filed no later than 28 days after entry of judgment, and is deemed denied if not ruled on within 60 days from its filing (M. R. Civ. P. 50(b))."
  edge-trial-judgment "Verdict or decision" -> post-trial { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 58" }
  edge-trial-settled "Settled before verdict" -> settled { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 41(a)" }
}

decision post-trial: "Post-trial motions" by applicant cite "M. R. Civ. P. 59"
{
  note "A motion for a new trial is filed no later than 28 days after entry of judgment and states in its heading the dates 60 and 120 days from its filing (M. R. Civ. P. 59(b)); opposing affidavits follow within 14 days after service (M. R. Civ. P. 59(c)); a motion to alter or amend is filed no later than 28 days after entry (M. R. Civ. P. 59(e)). Either motion not addressed in a written order within 60 days from filing is deemed denied, or within 120 days if the court extended the time (M. R. Civ. P. 59(f)). The court must not extend these times (M. R. Civ. P. 6(b)(2)). A timely motion under Rules 50(b), 52(b), 59 or 60(b) restarts the time to appeal from its disposition or deemed denial (M. R. App. P. 4(5)(a)(v))."
  edge-post-trial-resolved "Motions resolved or none filed" -> judgment-entered {
    authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 58"
  }
}

decision judgment-entered: "Final judgment entered" by office cite "M. R. Civ. P. 58"
{
  note "Every judgment is set out in a separate document; where one is required, judgment is entered when it is in the civil docket and set out in the separate document or 150 days have run (M. R. Civ. P. 58(a), (c)). A judgment is not final for appeal until any necessary determination of costs, attorney fees or sanctions is made (M. R. Civ. P. 58(e)). The prevailing party serves notice of entry within 14 days after entry (M. R. Civ. P. 77(d)). The clerk may tax costs on 14 days' notice, reviewable on motion served within the next 7 days; a motion for attorney fees is filed no later than 14 days after entry of judgment unless a statute or order provides otherwise (M. R. Civ. P. 54(d))."
  edge-judgment-entered-appeal "Notice of appeal within 30 days" -> appeal-taken {
    authority cite "M. R. App. P. 4(5)"
  }
  edge-judgment-entered-final "No appeal" -> final-no-appeal { authority cite "M. R. Civ. P. 58" }
}

terminal appeal-taken: "Appeal taken: continue in the Montana appellate package" outcome [appeal] cite "M. R. App. P. 4(5)"
{
  note "In civil cases the notice of appeal is filed with the clerk of the supreme court within 30 days from entry of the judgment, or 60 days where the United States, the State or a subdivision, officer or agency is a party; where notice of entry must be served under M. R. Civ. P. 77(d), the time runs from that service. Another party may cross-appeal within 15 days after the first notice or within the time otherwise prescribed, whichever expires last (M. R. App. P. 4(5)(a)). Hand-off to lit/mt-supreme (mt-supreme-court-civil-appeal)."
}

terminal final-no-appeal: "Final: no appeal" outcome [final] cite "M. R. Civ. P. 58"

terminal settled: "Settled: dismissed by stipulation" outcome [settlement] cite "M. R. Civ. P. 41(a)"
{
  note "The plaintiff may dismiss without a court order by a notice of dismissal before the opposing party serves an answer or a motion for summary judgment, or by a stipulation signed by all parties who have appeared; unless it states otherwise the dismissal is without prejudice (M. R. Civ. P. 41(a)(1))."
}
